---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import FeatureCard from '../components/FeatureCard.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<Hero />

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<span class="eyebrow">Why crust</span>
			<h2>Bash and TypeScript, one pipeline.</h2>
			<p class="section-lede">
				Shell stages and TS lambdas are equal citizens — both sit on the same pipeline. Pipe
				anything into anything: globs into HTTP, ranges into parallel workers, SQL rows
				into lambdas.
			</p>
			<div class="grid">
				<FeatureCard icon="🥖" title="Pipelines, first-class">
					<p>
						Every stage produces a stream — <code>Pipeline&lt;T&gt;</code>. Compose with
						<code>|</code> at the shell line or <code>.pipe()</code> in TypeScript.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
				<FeatureCard icon="🔁" title="HTTP verbs as stages">
					<p>
						<code>GET</code>, <code>POST</code>, <code>PUT</code>, <code>PATCH</code>,
						<code>DELETE</code> ship as pipeline stages — auto JSON encoding, headers via
						<code>-H</code>, status matchers like <code>expect 201</code> and
						<code>expect 2xx</code>.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
				<FeatureCard icon="🔗" title="Request chaining — capture">
					<p>
						<code>POST … | (r =&gt; r.json()) | capture ID (b =&gt; b.id)</code> — later
						lines expand <code>$ID</code>. Whole CRUD flows as <code>.pipes</code> suites,
						no framework.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
				<FeatureCard icon="⚡" title="Load scenarios & CI gates">
					<p>
						<code>load 30s 100/s | parallel 50 | GET :3000/health | stats | assert (s =&gt;
						s.p95 &lt; 200)</code> — paced ramps, honest drop accounting, thresholds as
						chained asserts.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
				<FeatureCard icon="🧪" title="Fixture testing & stress mode">
					<p>
						<code>test-fixture 'fixtures/*.crust.ts' -n1000 -j32</code> runs your
						<code>.crust.ts</code> fixtures with p50/p95/p99 reports.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
				<FeatureCard icon="🌐" title="OpenAPI mock, validator & proxy">
					<p>
						<code>mock-server ./openapi.yaml</code> — spec-driven mock with
						envelope-aware <code>--stateful</code> CRUD — persistent via <code>--state</code>
						sqlite/postgres, seedable via <code>--seed</code> — <code>--validate</code> 422s,
						and a <code>--proxy</code> mode that audits a real backend's conformance.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
				<FeatureCard icon="🤖" title="Agent skills, embedded">
					<p>
						<code>skills install</code> drops five Claude agent skills into
						<code>.claude/skills/</code> — grammar-lint-tested against the live parser, so
						examples can't rot.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
				<FeatureCard icon="🔗" title="Verify web links + SEO">
					<p>
						<code>verify-web-links https://example.com</code> — crawl your
						sitemap, catch broken links and dead anchors, diff Open Graph tags against
						fixtures.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
				<FeatureCard icon="🔌" title="One-liner mode">
					<p>
						Stay in your shell — call <code>crust -c '…'</code> from bash/zsh/fish for the
						lines where pipeline syntax wins.
					</p>
				</FeatureCard>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<span class="eyebrow">Recipes</span>
			<h2>From smoke tests to stress runs.</h2>
			<p class="section-lede">
				Hand-picked workflows you can lift into your own pipelines today.
			</p>
			<div class="recipe-grid">
				<a class="recipe" href="/docs/recipes/stress-testing/">
					<h3>Stress testing</h3>
					<p>
						Paced <code>load</code> scenarios with ramps and drop accounting — plus
						<code>--count</code> + <code>--threads</code> fixture runs at volume.
					</p>
					<span class="more">Read recipe →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="recipe" href="/docs/recipes/ci-load-gates/">
					<h3>CI load gates</h3>
					<p>
						<code>stats | assert (s =&gt; s.p95 &lt; 200)</code> — thresholds, baselines
						via <code>stats --out</code>, and honest exit codes for CI.
					</p>
					<span class="more">Read recipe →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="recipe" href="/docs/recipes/mock-server/">
					<h3>OpenAPI mock server</h3>
					<p>
						Boot a Bun.serve mock from any Swagger / OpenAPI 3.x spec — stateful CRUD
						that persists to sqlite/postgres, seeds itself on first boot, and
						round-trips enveloped entities.
					</p>
					<span class="more">Read recipe →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="recipe" href="/docs/recipes/api-smoke-tests/">
					<h3>API smoke tests</h3>
					<p>
						<code>read fixtures/*.json | POST :3000/users | expect 201</code> in one
						line — or whole <code>.pipes</code> suites with SQL asserts.
					</p>
					<span class="more">Read recipe →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="recipe" href="/docs/recipes/log-mining/">
					<h3>Log mining</h3>
					<p>
						Forensic queries over log trees, live streams from any command via
						<code>stdin</code>, and an interactive <code>logs</code> session that
						holds the stream while you iterate on filters.
					</p>
					<span class="more">Read recipe →</span>
				</a>
				<a class="recipe" href="/docs/recipes/heap-snapshots/">
					<h3>Heap snapshots during testing</h3>
					<p>
						A Bun <code>[test].preload</code> that writes a
						<code>.heapsnapshot</code> and prints rss / heap / top-classes after every
						<code>bun test</code>.
					</p>
					<span class="more">Read recipe →</span>
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section cta">
		<div class="container cta-inner">
			<h2>Bake it in.</h2>
			<p>
				Install in one curl. Script it with <code>.crust</code> files, drive it from your
				shell with <code>crust -c</code>, or live in the REPL.
			</p>
			<div class="cta-actions">
				<a class="btn primary" href="/docs/intro/">Get started</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.section {
		padding: 4rem 0 2rem;
	}
	.section h2 {
		max-width: 24ch;
	}
	.section-lede {
		color: var(--fg-muted);
		max-width: 60ch;
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
	}
	.grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
	}
	.recipe-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
	}
	.recipe {
		display: block;
		background: var(--bg-soft);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
		padding: 1.5rem 1.4rem;
		color: var(--fg);
		transition: all 0.2s ease;
	}
	.recipe:hover {
		border-color: var(--accent);
		transform: translateY(-2px);
		color: var(--fg);
	}
	.recipe h3 {
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
	}
	.recipe p {
		color: var(--fg-muted);
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}
	.recipe .more {
		color: var(--accent);
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
	.recipe code {
		font-size: 0.82em;
	}

	.cta {
		padding: 5rem 0 4rem;
	}
	.cta-inner {
		background: linear-gradient(120deg, var(--bg-soft) 0%, var(--bg-elevated) 100%);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
		padding: 3rem 2rem;
		text-align: center;
	}
	.cta-inner h2 {
		max-width: none;
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	}
	.cta-inner p {
		color: var(--fg-muted);
		max-width: 48ch;
		margin: 0 auto 1.75rem;
	}
	.cta-actions {
		display: flex;
		gap: 0.6rem;
		justify-content: center;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}
	.btn {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 0.7rem 1.1rem;
		border-radius: 8px;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		transition: all 0.15s ease;
	}
	.btn.primary {
		background: linear-gradient(120deg, var(--accent) 0%, var(--accent-2) 100%);
		color: var(--bg);
		border-color: transparent;
	}
	.btn.primary:hover {
		transform: translateY(-1px);
		box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(231, 169, 85, 0.35);
		color: var(--bg);
	}
	.btn.ghost {
		color: var(--fg);
		background: var(--bg-soft);
	}
	.btn.ghost:hover {
		border-color: var(--accent);
		color: var(--accent);
	}
</style>
